    LLM: "Play tight and value strong hands; fold weak hands. Position matters: acting later allows you to see others' actions first.\n\nUse bluffing sparingly; balance your range so opponents cannot read you. Consider pot odds when calling or raising.\n\nAdjust to opponents' tendencies and table dynamics; exploit predictable players. Psychological reads matter in home-game variants.",
